{"slug":"kaido-racer-2","title":"Kaido Racer 2","desc":"PS2, Genki 2006 (Europe)","notes":["Genki games: the car models were decoded from scratch (the format has no public description).","Folder names are the number of the game's archive entry (no car names are known).  One car = the first (most detailed) of its levels of detail.","The car file is a tree of parts and holds EVERY variant of the shop (5 bodies, 5 front bumpers, several bonnets, wings ...); the variants of a part sit on the same place.  The car here is the stock set: the first variant of every part, each part at its place in the tree.  Moving parts (pop-up headlights) are in their closed position.  The game's hull / shadow volumes are left out.","Textures: the pictures of the game's body-part file (body, bumpers, grilles, lamps, decals); the cars of Racing Battle and Tokyo Xtreme Racer 3 come with the livery of the file, Kaido Racer / Drift with the plain white body picture (the game colours the car at run time).  Parts without a picture have the game's own material colour (black interior, tinted glass ...).","No wheels: they are separate models in the game.  The game's wheels are in the folder _Rims (most detailed version only).","Left out on purpose: stickers and number plates that the game textures at run time (blank white cards), light-glow sprites and reflection layers (Kaido Racer 1 / 2, Drift), the 4 cards behind the wheels of Kaido Racer 1.","The game's triangle strips run on from one piece to another without a break.  Racing Battle C1 GP and Kaido Racer 2 mark the joins in the vertex data (see below); Kaido Racer 1, Drift and TXR3 do not, there the converter removes a join when the two triangles around a long edge do not form a flat quad with continuous normals, or when a long triangle contradicts the normals of its corners (real long slivers such as door sills and roof bands are kept).","Its files glue pieces of 3 to 10 vertices from all over the car into one strip (two triangles out of five are joins that cross the cabin).  Every vertex carries the game's 'draw no triangle here' bit (the PS2 ADC flag: the lowest bit of its height, or for meshes without normals the strip flag byte / the lowest bit of the vertex colour alpha): the joins are removed exactly as the game skips them (rebuilt 2026-11-20, cars and rims; before that a geometric guess left crumpled bumpers and streaks)."],"tags":["kaido-racer-2"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["00046","",484435,"kaido-racer-2","car-00046.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00046.webp"],["00068","",419401,"kaido-racer-2","car-00068.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00068.webp"],["00079","",428006,"kaido-racer-2","car-00079.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00079.webp"],["00090","",427153,"kaido-racer-2","car-00090.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00090.webp"],["00101","",398278,"kaido-racer-2","car-00101.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00101.webp"],["00112","",394878,"kaido-racer-2","car-00112.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00112.webp"],["00123","",469629,"kaido-racer-2","car-00123.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00123.webp"],["00134","",420526,"kaido-racer-2","car-00134.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00134.webp"],["00145","",350949,"kaido-racer-2","car-00145.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00145.webp"],["00156","",344303,"kaido-racer-2","car-00156.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00156.webp"],["00167","",334625,"kaido-racer-2","car-00167.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00167.webp"],["00178","",364377,"kaido-racer-2","car-00178.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00178.webp"],["00189","",392375,"kaido-racer-2","car-00189.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00189.webp"],["00200","",417103,"kaido-racer-2","car-00200.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00200.webp"],["00211","",461320,"kaido-racer-2","car-00211.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00211.webp"],["00222","",374292,"kaido-racer-2","car-00222.zip","thumbs/kaido-racer-2/cars/car-00222.webp"],["00233",